<p>I find the recovery story of the messianic schizophrenic extremely cliché and unnecessary. Also, by the time the research staff used the pen for their own purposes, the Foundation was already suspecting that it had the power to <em>make a company appear out of nowhere</em> - Isn’t it weird that access to it wasn’t forbidden to people who weren’t absolutely dependable? These things worsen what is otherwise a good article :-/</p>
<p>On the other hand, the presentation of the anomaly, the slow buildup of the test logs, and the exploration of the implications are all really good. The reading was engaging and interesting. You've taken a simple concept and executed it surprisingly well, take your +1</p>

