														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4072754">
									

<blockquote>
<p>I find the recovery story of the messianic schizophrenic extremely cliché and unnecessary</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I can definitely understand that. My main goals with the discovery was to make something that (1) made more sense than the original one<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-345296-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-345296-1')">1</a></sup> and (2) also explained why the previous possessor wouldn't also take advantage of it the artifact and destroy/significantly alter the world. Mentally ill person seemed like a reasonable out.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Isn’t it weird that access to it wasn’t forbidden to people who weren’t absolutely dependable</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was originally going to try for an ending that banked more on the idea that &quot;power corrupts&quot;, but it didn't really end up that way. I'll probably revisit the ending after a few months of a break from this thing and can reapproach it with a fresh mind.</p>
<p>Though,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>it had the power to <em>make a company appear out of nowhere</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>It only created a legal entity with a given name. It doesn't affect the physical world, it couldn't give that company a bunch of employees and an office building.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-345296-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-345296-1')">1</a>. When the SCP was still in the sandbox.</div>
</div>

